g forward  videos this was a month where i finally  for the first time in a long time was  able to do six half-hour hegel videos  and make some good progress through the  phenomenology that we are reaching the  end of you know i've been doing this  half hour hegel project for seven and a  half years now  so you know it's time to bring it to a  successful conclusion but the only way  is through plowing through  all of these videos there is also of  course the speculative fiction  uh videos that i i started doing this  month some on ursula k le guin not on  uh a wizard of earthsea quite yet but i  did do two earthsea stories and her from  elf land to poughkeepsie and i did some  on philip jose farmer's the lovers as  well very famous science fiction story  almost infamous for some people who  thought it was smut  we talk about why that's not actually  the case i did a book review i was  hoping to get to more but i i wasn't  able to do  more than that i also did a video  compiling the i would tell a joke and  then they say something about a  philosopher  from twitter  i did a video as well for stoicon 2021  so if you want to know what's going on  with stoicon watch that video i'll link  to it below  and uh everybody's invited and you can  you can donate as much or as little as  you'd like it's an online event it's  open to everybody  i cannot recommend it highly enough to  you because we've got a really amazing  lineup of speakers workshop providers  panelists and it's going to be really  quite  uh we i released two wisdom for life  show recording videos that's my radio  show that i do with dan hayes  i also did a sadler's stories one that's  a little bit gruesome about getting my  wisdom teeth pulled and i managed to get  a few core concept videos done in  particular those on michelle foucault  and he has the subject in power which  i'll be continuing uh this coming month  podcast i i released quite a few podcast  episodes in the sadler's lectures  podcast on simone d